Package: rfriend
Type: Package
Title: Batch Statistical Tests with Assumption Checks and Reports
Version: 3.2.1
Authors@R: c(person("Sander H.", "van Delden", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "plantmind@proton.me"))
Description: Wraps common statistical procedures in user-friendly 'f_'
    functions that check model assumptions, transform the response when
    needed, run post hoc tests and write publication-ready reports to the
    console, 'pdf', 'Microsoft Word', 'Microsoft Excel' or 'R Markdown'.
    Several response variables can be analysed in one call, and post hoc
    results are summarised with a compact letter display. Tests include
    analysis of variance f_aov(), linear regression f_lm(), linear
    mixed-effects models f_lmer() (based on 'lme4' and 'lmerTest'),
    generalised linear models f_glm(), t-tests f_t_test(), Wilcoxon tests
    f_wilcox_test(), Kruskal-Wallis tests f_kruskal_test(), Friedman tests
    f_friedman() and chi-square tests f_chisq_test(). The function
    f_stat_wizard() inspects the data and recommends a suitable test as
    ready-to-run code. Data exploration tools include f_summary(), f_scan(),
    f_corplot(), f_boxplot(), f_hist() and f_qqnorm(), outlier handling with
    f_outliers() and f_remove_outliers(), and transformations with
    f_boxcox() (based on 'MASS' and 'rcompanion') and f_bestNormalize()
    (extending 'bestNormalize'). Models can be compared with
    f_model_compare(). Utilities such as f_clear(), f_setwd(), f_factors(),
    f_long() and f_example_data() simplify everyday tasks in R.
License: GPL-3
